00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:14,740
(Watch on KonFlix.vip)

1
00:00:04,651 --> 00:00:06,403
THE FOLLOWING CONTENT CONTAINS DEPICTIONS
OF DOMESTIC ABUSE.

2
00:00:06,486 --> 00:00:07,571
VIEWER DISCRETION IS ADVISED.

3
00:00:07,654 --> 00:00:10,657
[Heeju breathing heavily]

4
00:00:12,117 --> 00:00:13,327
Aren't you tired? Huh?

5
00:00:14,119 --> 00:00:15,370
Why don't you come sit down?

6
00:00:15,454 --> 00:00:17,039
Let's talk a little
and figure this out.

7
00:00:17,122 --> 00:00:20,792
[Heeju breathing heavily]

8
00:00:20,876 --> 00:00:24,129
If you give me the gold bar
and the knife, we can talk.

9
00:00:24,212 --> 00:00:25,756
Ugh, you're being really annoying.

10
00:00:27,299 --> 00:00:28,633
[exhales]

11
00:00:28,717 --> 00:00:31,636
[panicked breathing]

12
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:33,513
[gold bars clanging]

13
00:00:33,597 --> 00:00:35,349
Closer.

14
00:00:37,142 --> 00:00:39,061
[scraping across floor]

15
00:00:39,895 --> 00:00:40,896
And the knife.

16
00:00:45,942 --> 00:00:47,152
[clatters]

17
00:00:49,863 --> 00:00:52,741
[panicked breathing]

18
00:00:52,824 --> 00:00:55,202
[exhales sharply]

19
00:00:56,995 --> 00:00:58,163
[relieved exhale]

20
00:00:58,246 --> 00:01:01,625
[Woogy] You need to think about this
from an economic perspective, okay?

21
00:01:01,708 --> 00:01:04,503
It really doesn't matter
if it's gold or drugs.

22
00:01:04,586 --> 00:01:07,297
[Woogy] All that matters
is raking in the dough.

23
00:01:07,381 --> 00:01:09,299
Can we turn that item into money or not?

24
00:01:09,383 --> 00:01:12,636
You really think taking the gold bar
to a jewelry shop's a good idea?

25
00:01:12,719 --> 00:01:15,097
[Woogy] A 10-kilogram bar
with a foreign stamp on it?

26
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:16,556
[exhales]

27
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:18,558
Okay, just listen.

28
00:01:18,642 --> 00:01:22,145
The jewelry shops, the pawn shops even,
they're all linked to who I work for.

29
00:01:22,229 --> 00:01:25,023
[Woogy] Stuff like gold bars,
that's gonna get around.

30
00:01:25,107 --> 00:01:27,317
You wanna sell a gold bar,
you gotta hand over your phone number,

31
00:01:27,401 --> 00:01:29,236
name, and ID.
So what?

32
00:01:29,319 --> 00:01:31,446
You'll write down,
"Kim Heeju, ID 123?"

33
00:01:31,530 --> 00:01:34,616
You think you can handle all this alone?
You can't.

34
00:01:34,700 --> 00:01:36,535
But I can.
I'm telling you.

35
00:01:36,618 --> 00:01:37,953
My methods are solid.

36
00:01:41,164 --> 00:01:42,541
How do we do it, then?

37
00:01:42,624 --> 00:01:44,835
[exhales sharply]
You a bit more interested now?

38
00:01:44,918 --> 00:01:48,338
Okay, before I lay all this out,
let's make a deal.

39
00:01:48,422 --> 00:01:50,382
-Hey, get back!
-[Woogy] Like partners.

40
00:01:50,465 --> 00:01:52,134
[Heeju] I said get back. Go.

41
00:01:52,217 --> 00:01:53,468
Talk from there.

42
00:01:53,552 --> 00:01:54,845
[exhales sharply]

43
00:01:58,181 --> 00:02:00,851
[Woogy mumbling]

44
00:02:02,269 --> 00:02:04,896
Okay, first, where's the casket?

45
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:06,773
[Woogy] This can't be everything.

46
00:02:08,024 --> 00:02:09,109
Just tell me where it is.

47
00:02:09,192 --> 00:02:10,944
I need to know exactly
how many bars there are

48
00:02:11,027 --> 00:02:12,112
before I can put a plan together.

49
00:02:12,195 --> 00:02:14,156
Why should I even trust you?

50
00:02:15,449 --> 00:02:16,950
I literally just told you!

51
00:02:17,784 --> 00:02:19,995
If I was gonna rat you out to the boss,
I would have done it already,

52
00:02:20,078 --> 00:02:21,246
and all the guys would be here.

53
00:02:23,749 --> 00:02:26,585
Fine, I wasn't gonna tell you this.
Guess I have to, though.

54
00:02:28,253 --> 00:02:29,463
Look.

55
00:02:29,546 --> 00:02:32,215
[Woogy] That shit hurt.
It still hurts.

56
00:02:33,008 --> 00:02:35,719
They were gonna cut off my ear
if I didn't start talking.

57
00:02:35,802 --> 00:02:37,179
But I held out.

58
00:02:37,262 --> 00:02:40,265
[Woogy] You know why?
'Cause I thought of you.

59
00:02:40,348 --> 00:02:41,933
[exhales]
What the hell?

60
00:02:42,017 --> 00:02:43,727
Why am I such a softie?

61
00:02:43,810 --> 00:02:45,353
[Heeju] Don't make me laugh.

62
00:02:45,437 --> 00:02:48,356
The only reason you showed up here
was to look for the drugs.

63
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:50,275
If you couldn't find them
you would have threatened me

64
00:02:50,358 --> 00:02:52,319
or done whatever it took
to make me talk.

65
00:02:52,402 --> 00:02:54,321
And once you found them,
you would have killed me.

66
00:02:54,404 --> 00:02:56,448
Oh, really?
Correct me if I'm wrong here,

67
00:02:56,531 --> 00:02:58,867
but you were the one threatening
to shoot me.

68
00:03:00,702 --> 00:03:03,163
Okay, I get it.
Let's move on.

69
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:05,165
[Woogy] How about this?

70
00:03:05,248 --> 00:03:07,083
Don't tell me where to find the gold.

71
00:03:07,167 --> 00:03:08,585
[Woogy] I won't ask, either.

72
00:03:09,252 --> 00:03:10,253
If you think I'd kill you

73
00:03:10,337 --> 00:03:13,423
and make a run for it after finding out
where the gold is, don't tell me.

74
00:03:13,507 --> 00:03:15,467
[Woogy] If I have no idea,
there's no problem, right?

75
00:03:15,550 --> 00:03:17,093
Instead, how's this?

76
00:03:18,220 --> 00:03:20,430
Every three days,
you give me one gold bar.

77
00:03:20,514 --> 00:03:23,767
[Woogy] Then it'll be up to me
to sell it and bring you the cash.

78
00:03:23,850 --> 00:03:25,685
That means I won't be able
to pull anything funny

79
00:03:25,769 --> 00:03:26,853
until we've sold all the gold.

80
00:03:26,937 --> 00:03:28,021
Make sense?

81
00:03:30,023 --> 00:03:31,024
[Woogy] How many are there?

82
00:03:31,107 --> 00:03:32,609
That I need to know.

83
00:03:32,692 --> 00:03:35,695
[strained breathing]

84
00:03:37,864 --> 00:03:38,865
There's ten.

85
00:03:44,704 --> 00:03:45,789
[Woogy] Ten?

86
00:03:45,872 --> 00:03:50,210
If we sell one for a billion,
times ten is ten billion.

87
00:03:50,293 --> 00:03:51,378
Split it in half.

88
00:03:51,461 --> 00:03:52,629
-[Woogy] Five billion each.
-Split it?

89
00:03:52,712 --> 00:03:53,922
[exhales]

90
00:03:54,839 --> 00:03:56,800
[Heeju] You think it's just you and me?
STYLE
::cue()

91
00:03:56,883 --> 00:03:59,886
It's not our gold.
It belongs to Dokyung.

92
00:03:59,970 --> 00:04:01,096
What? Lee Dokyung?

93
00:04:01,179 --> 00:04:02,722
Nah, he's gonna die soon.

94
00:04:02,806 --> 00:04:05,308
[Woogy] And even if he lives,
he's going to jail anyway.

95
00:04:05,392 --> 00:04:07,185
Wait, why not just cut him out?

96
00:04:07,269 --> 00:04:08,645
What'd you say?

97
00:04:09,563 --> 00:04:10,897
Oh.

98
00:04:12,107 --> 00:04:13,108
What, are you dating?

99
00:04:14,025 --> 00:04:16,236
Am I right?
Is he your boyfriend?

100
00:04:16,319 --> 00:04:18,405
-[groans]
-[Woogy] Eh, doesn't matter.

101
00:04:18,488 --> 00:04:20,156
How is it Lee Dokyung's?

102
00:04:20,240 --> 00:04:21,658
You realize he stole it, right?

103
00:04:21,741 --> 00:04:23,326
So it really belongs to Chairman An.

104
00:04:24,077 --> 00:04:25,161
[Heeju] Okay, then.

105
00:04:26,955 --> 00:04:29,082
[Heeju] So the three of us will split it.

106
00:04:29,165 --> 00:04:30,959
You'll get exactly one-third of the money.

107
00:04:31,042 --> 00:04:32,210
That's your share.

108
00:04:33,420 --> 00:04:34,421
Okay.

109
00:04:34,963 --> 00:04:35,964
Okay!

110
00:04:37,424 --> 00:04:38,425
[exhales sharply]

111
00:04:38,508 --> 00:04:40,635
-So, then.
-[Heeju] What?

112
00:04:40,719 --> 00:04:42,971
-[Woogy] We should fist bump so that...
-Don't come any closer!

113
00:04:43,054 --> 00:04:45,348
Well, we gotta lock in our contract, so...

114
00:04:46,725 --> 00:04:47,851
...fist bump to seal the deal.

115
00:04:49,352 --> 00:04:51,897
First you have to tell me how you plan
on selling the gold bars.

116
00:04:52,355 --> 00:04:53,815
Explain that.
Then I'll decide.

117
00:04:53,899 --> 00:04:55,358
[exhales sharply]
Are you serious?

118
00:04:56,401 --> 00:04:57,402
What the...

119
00:04:58,528 --> 00:05:00,614
[Woogy] Fine. Listen carefully.

120
00:05:00,697 --> 00:05:05,035
[Woogy] Gold is traded in hundreds
of forms in shops across the country.

121
00:05:05,118 --> 00:05:07,787
Gold rings, gold pigs, random stuff.

122
00:05:07,871 --> 00:05:09,873
And the gold bar.

123
00:05:09,956 --> 00:05:14,461
The one-kilogram bars are the easiest ones
for us to trade.

124
00:05:14,544 --> 00:05:18,423
Everything changes depending on
the weight, purity,

125
00:05:18,506 --> 00:05:19,883
and where it was manufactured.

126
00:05:19,966 --> 00:05:23,887
So first we gotta break these down
into one-kilo bars

127
00:05:23,970 --> 00:05:25,555
-and recast them.
-[Heeju] Who can do that?

128
00:05:26,473 --> 00:05:28,475
-[Heeju] You?
-[Woogy] No.

129
00:05:28,558 --> 00:05:30,727
We'll obviously need a goldsmith for that.

130
00:05:30,810 --> 00:05:32,729
Then there's the actual sale.

131
00:05:32,812 --> 00:05:35,273
Selling a 10-kilo bar would be hard,

132
00:05:35,357 --> 00:05:36,942
but small ones, well,

133
00:05:37,025 --> 00:05:39,110
jewelry stores have
no problem buying those.

134
00:05:40,028 --> 00:05:43,239
All of Gwangwon-do has ties to our company
so that won't work.

135
00:05:43,323 --> 00:05:45,408
I'll have to go to jewelry stores
in other areas

136
00:05:45,492 --> 00:05:47,744
and sell only one bar per store.

137
00:05:47,827 --> 00:05:50,121
The whole process of recasting
a bar to selling it

138
00:05:50,205 --> 00:05:53,416
shouldn't take any more than, say,
three days.

139
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:56,044
So selling them all should take a month.

140
00:05:56,127 --> 00:05:57,921
And to avoid being tracked by the cops,

141
00:05:58,004 --> 00:06:00,382
we gotta make all
of our transactions in cash.

142
00:06:00,465 --> 00:06:03,635
Not to mention, we'll need fake IDs,
burner phones, and burner bank accounts.

143
00:06:03,718 --> 00:06:07,138
But I'll be taking care of all that,
so don't you worry about a thing.

144
00:06:07,222 --> 00:06:08,890
SAMJIN GOLD EXCHANGE

145
00:06:11,935 --> 00:06:15,230
And Heeju,
let's make one thing clear.

146
00:06:17,023 --> 00:06:19,317
[Woogy] Until we've sold all ten gold bars
and split the cash,

147
00:06:19,401 --> 00:06:20,819
we trust each other.

148
00:06:22,862 --> 00:06:26,157
[Woogy] Never, seriously never...

149
00:06:27,117 --> 00:06:30,495
Ever, ever, ever,
never betray each other.

150
00:06:30,578 --> 00:06:32,998
[Woogy] Do you promise?
If not, we're both dead.

151
00:06:33,957 --> 00:06:36,835
You'll be discovered in that mining town
hanging from your neck.

152
00:06:36,918 --> 00:06:38,712
And as for me,
I'm screwing the company over, too,

153
00:06:38,795 --> 00:06:42,424
so I'll get something chopped off
and become a cripple.

154
00:06:45,135 --> 00:06:46,428
You know what I'm saying?

155
00:06:47,762 --> 00:06:48,763
[exhales]

156
00:06:50,682 --> 00:06:52,434
You're the one I'm worried about.

157
00:06:52,517 --> 00:06:53,852
[exhales]

158
00:06:57,188 --> 00:06:58,231
[exhales sharply]

159
00:06:58,314 --> 00:06:59,816
[Woogy] Okay.

160
00:07:00,692 --> 00:07:01,943
[Woogy grunts]

161
00:07:03,653 --> 00:07:05,071
Do this to sign the contract.

162
00:07:05,155 --> 00:07:07,323
Hmm? Deal?

163
00:07:13,371 --> 00:07:15,707
You gotta say "deal" when you do it.
That's how it works.

164
00:07:15,790 --> 00:07:17,125
Deal.

165
00:07:17,208 --> 00:07:18,251
[scoffs]

166
00:07:21,963 --> 00:07:22,964
Deal.

167
00:07:24,132 --> 00:07:25,383
[exhales sharply]

168
00:07:28,136 --> 00:07:29,137
[exhales]

169
00:07:29,220 --> 00:07:30,221
[Woogy] Finally.

170
00:07:32,932 --> 00:07:35,935
[♪ tense music]
STYLE
::cue()

171
00:07:53,578 --> 00:07:56,581
[♪ tense music continues]

172
00:08:13,848 --> 00:08:16,559
[crows cawing]

173
00:08:16,643 --> 00:08:21,356
EPISODE 3
PARTNERSHIP

174
00:08:21,439 --> 00:08:22,440
[Jinman] Yeah.

175
00:08:25,985 --> 00:08:27,445
[clears throat]

176
00:08:27,529 --> 00:08:29,989
[Jinman groans]
Goodness.

177
00:08:30,073 --> 00:08:31,449
[Jinman clears throat]

178
00:08:31,533 --> 00:08:33,618
[metal creaking]

179
00:08:36,371 --> 00:08:38,998
[chains rattling]

180
00:08:39,916 --> 00:08:42,001
[Jinman] Careful.
Ugh, shit.

181
00:08:42,085 --> 00:08:43,461
[camera shutter clicks]

182
00:08:44,671 --> 00:08:46,172
SEOYOON, YERIN, I'M SORRY FOR GOING FIRST.
TO EVERYONE WHO WAS HARMED BECAUSE OF ME,

183
00:08:46,256 --> 00:08:47,715
I AM SORRY. THIS IS THE LAST CHOICE
I CAN MAKE. I'M SORRY. I'M SO SORRY.

184
00:08:49,342 --> 00:08:50,343
Hold up. Stop.

185
00:08:57,350 --> 00:08:58,518
[camera shutter clicks]

186
00:09:00,812 --> 00:09:02,981
[indistinct chatter]

187
00:09:05,066 --> 00:09:06,192
Go, yeah.

188
00:09:08,278 --> 00:09:09,362
Should I send him to forensics?

189
00:09:09,445 --> 00:09:10,822
Nah, just the morgue is fine.

190
00:09:10,905 --> 00:09:11,990
-Yes, sir.
-Yeah.

191
00:09:12,073 --> 00:09:13,408
-[Male Police Officer] The morgue.
-[groans]

192
00:09:13,491 --> 00:09:15,243
[clicks tongue, clears throat]

193
00:09:15,326 --> 00:09:18,329
[cell phone vibrating]

194
00:09:19,664 --> 00:09:21,416
-Take him to the morgue.
-[Male Police Officer] Understood.

195
00:09:21,499 --> 00:09:25,378
[cell phone vibrating]

196
00:09:25,461 --> 00:09:26,504
[exhales]

197
00:09:28,798 --> 00:09:30,884
Ah, I did it. Yeah.

198
00:09:30,967 --> 00:09:33,094
I took care of it like you asked.

199
00:09:33,178 --> 00:09:34,888
Who wrote that note, though?

200
00:09:36,097 --> 00:09:37,891
Looked like President Go's handwriting.

201
00:09:39,893 --> 00:09:41,936
You gotta stop with all
these useless theatrics.

202
00:09:42,020 --> 00:09:44,439
It's a waste.
Just keep your guys in line.

203
00:09:45,565 --> 00:09:46,649
[Hocheol] Thanks for your work.

204
00:09:47,817 --> 00:09:49,402
See you soon, Detective.

205
00:09:49,485 --> 00:09:50,528
Sounds good.

206
00:09:51,404 --> 00:09:52,405
[cell phone beeps]

207
00:09:52,488 --> 00:09:55,283
GANGWON SAEBAEK HOSPITAL

208
00:09:55,366 --> 00:09:57,952
[machine rumbling]

209
00:10:06,252 --> 00:10:07,587
[Sunok exhales]

210
00:10:07,670 --> 00:10:09,464
What the hell have we been doing all day?

211
00:10:10,131 --> 00:10:12,050
We left the shop unattended.

212
00:10:12,133 --> 00:10:13,426
[Female Nurse] Ms. Yeo Sunok.

213
00:10:13,509 --> 00:10:15,345
Here. Come on.

214
00:10:22,477 --> 00:10:23,686
[Male Doctor grunts]

215
00:10:24,604 --> 00:10:25,897
[Male Doctor] Hello.

216
00:10:25,980 --> 00:10:27,440
Could the patient wait outside?

217
00:10:27,523 --> 00:10:29,275
I'd like to speak with the guardian first.

218
00:10:29,359 --> 00:10:32,111
-Uh...
-You can just talk.

219
00:10:32,195 --> 00:10:33,696
I already know anyway.

220
00:10:34,697 --> 00:10:36,032
[all exhaling sharply]

221
00:10:37,450 --> 00:10:41,663
You were diagnosed here a year ago,
but you never went to another hospital?

222
00:10:41,746 --> 00:10:43,456
-No.
-[Male Doctor groans]

223
00:10:43,539 --> 00:10:45,375
[Male Doctor] We should
have started treatment then.

224
00:10:45,458 --> 00:10:46,918
We're a little late now.

225
00:10:47,919 --> 00:10:49,045
If you look here,

226
00:10:49,128 --> 00:10:52,340
you'll see that the tumor cells
have metastasized to the lungs.

227
00:10:52,423 --> 00:10:53,633
[Sunok grunts]

228
00:10:53,716 --> 00:10:56,719
[Male Doctor] Were you feeling okay?
I imagine the pain would be quite severe.

229
00:10:57,971 --> 00:11:00,181
Could surgery be an option?

230
00:11:00,265 --> 00:11:02,016
She should get hospitalized first.

231
00:11:02,767 --> 00:11:04,227
I recommend an examination,

232
00:11:04,310 --> 00:11:06,771
then beginning chemotherapy
to slow down the metastasis.

233
00:11:06,854 --> 00:11:08,940
[Male Doctor] As for surgery,

234
00:11:09,023 --> 00:11:11,317
let's see how things progress
and then decide.

235
00:11:11,901 --> 00:11:14,570
-'Kay.
-So my cancer's in the final stage.

236
00:11:14,654 --> 00:11:16,364
Wouldn't surgery be useless?

237
00:11:16,447 --> 00:11:19,158
[Male Doctor exhales sharply]
Well, when it comes to stages,

238
00:11:19,242 --> 00:11:20,326
you could say that, however...

239
00:11:20,410 --> 00:11:21,536
How much longer do I have?

240
00:11:21,619 --> 00:11:24,747
A specific time frame
is hard to determine at this point.

241
00:11:24,831 --> 00:11:26,791
If I get treatment, I can live...

242
00:11:27,375 --> 00:11:28,710
...how much longer?
Into my 80s?

243
00:11:28,793 --> 00:11:31,671
-Auntie.
-[Sunok] I knew it'd be like this.

244
00:11:31,754 --> 00:11:33,256
They wanna fill me with drugs...

245
00:11:33,923 --> 00:11:36,301
...and poke me with needles even though
I'm dying anyway.

246
00:11:36,384 --> 00:11:39,679
That's how hospitals make money, isn't it?
Hey, we're leaving.

247
00:11:39,762 --> 00:11:41,014
-Auntie!
-Get up. I'm done with all this.

248
00:11:41,097 --> 00:11:42,974
Auntie, please wait! Seriously!

249
00:11:44,225 --> 00:11:45,226
[exhales sharply]
STYLE
::cue()

250
00:11:46,769 --> 00:11:48,896
-Auntie.
-Just forget it.

251
00:11:48,980 --> 00:11:51,232
Oh, come on, please!

252
00:11:51,316 --> 00:11:52,734
I said forget it!

253
00:11:52,817 --> 00:11:54,569
These guys are all crooks.

254
00:11:54,652 --> 00:11:56,487
They don't deserve our hard-earned money.

255
00:11:56,571 --> 00:11:59,115
If this is really about the money,
don't worry.

256
00:11:59,198 --> 00:12:00,908
-I have it.
-[Sunok] Where? Show me.

257
00:12:00,992 --> 00:12:02,493
I wanna see some before I die.

258
00:12:02,577 --> 00:12:05,246
[groaning]

259
00:12:06,831 --> 00:12:08,583
Aren't you in a lot of pain right now?

260
00:12:09,292 --> 00:12:11,794
This is about more than
just you living longer.

261
00:12:11,878 --> 00:12:13,880
Come on.
You're not dead yet.

262
00:12:13,963 --> 00:12:17,050
At least let them give you something
to ease the pain while you're still alive.

263
00:12:18,468 --> 00:12:20,261
Since when did you worry
about me like this?

264
00:12:21,721 --> 00:12:23,264
You were the one who ran off
to live your own life.

265
00:12:25,558 --> 00:12:29,103
And now that I'm dying,
you suddenly have a sense of duty?

266
00:12:29,187 --> 00:12:31,731
You're the one who needs to have
a sense of duty.

267
00:12:31,814 --> 00:12:35,318
What kind of mother wants to just die
and leave their kid by themself?

268
00:12:37,487 --> 00:12:38,780
Am I your mother?

269
00:12:39,655 --> 00:12:40,656
Well, aren't you?

270
00:12:41,491 --> 00:12:43,659
You gave birth to me.

271
00:12:48,456 --> 00:12:50,083
[Sunok] You think I had you
'cause I wanted to?

272
00:12:51,876 --> 00:12:52,960
[exhales sharply]

273
00:12:56,255 --> 00:12:57,382
[sighs]

274
00:13:04,347 --> 00:13:07,350
[bus engine rumbling]

275
00:13:40,675 --> 00:13:43,678
[engine revving]

276
00:13:43,761 --> 00:13:49,684
WELCOME TO GOLD LAND
THE CITY OF DREAMS AND HOPES

277
00:13:50,601 --> 00:13:53,229
[Jinman groans]

278
00:13:54,355 --> 00:13:56,899
[humming]

279
00:13:56,983 --> 00:13:57,984
Hey.

280
00:14:01,237 --> 00:14:03,447
Yeah...

281
00:14:04,115 --> 00:14:07,285
[Jinman] What's this?
I expected a nice spread.

282
00:14:07,368 --> 00:14:10,246
[Jinman] Ah, come on.
Guess not.

283
00:14:10,329 --> 00:14:12,081
So disappointing.

284
00:14:13,457 --> 00:14:16,335
[Jinman] Anyway, I guess the chairman
isn't back from overseas.

285
00:14:17,378 --> 00:14:18,588
I must say, you're looking great.

286
00:14:19,922 --> 00:14:21,716
[Jinman] It must be fun playing
the chairman.

287
00:14:21,799 --> 00:14:23,509
[Hocheol] Lee Dokyung's cell phone.

288
00:14:23,593 --> 00:14:25,219
[Hocheol] Same guy you were tracking
a few days ago.

289
00:14:25,303 --> 00:14:27,597
-Does that mean he's dead?
-[Hocheol] No, he's in the hospital.

290
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:29,682
But now the cops are on his tail.

291
00:14:29,765 --> 00:14:31,392
Hence our little meeting here.

292
00:14:31,475 --> 00:14:34,312
Not much I can do.
Not if the police are on him. No way.

293
00:14:34,395 --> 00:14:36,147
I'm not asking you to do anything
to Lee Dokyung.

294
00:14:37,773 --> 00:14:41,068
Just take this phone
and use it to find a person.

295
00:14:43,321 --> 00:14:45,156
No way he's working alone.

296
00:14:46,324 --> 00:14:47,325
He's got an accomplice.

297
00:14:48,284 --> 00:14:51,996
A stupid fuck who took off with
the van carrying all of our stuff.

298
00:14:52,079 --> 00:14:53,122
[inhales]

299
00:14:54,081 --> 00:14:55,541
Ah, the casket.

300
00:14:56,417 --> 00:14:57,919
Ah, that must be a headache.

301
00:14:58,920 --> 00:15:02,632
Just dig through his calls and texts
and see what you can find.

302
00:15:02,715 --> 00:15:05,676
You can't expect me to do all that.
Come on.

303
00:15:05,760 --> 00:15:08,095
Searching through
a phone like that's illegal.

304
00:15:08,179 --> 00:15:09,639
And it takes too much time.

305
00:15:10,848 --> 00:15:13,142
Too much money, too.

306
00:15:13,226 --> 00:15:14,727
I'll give you the money,
so don't worry.

307
00:15:14,810 --> 00:15:15,978
[Jinman] Oh, yeah.

308
00:15:16,062 --> 00:15:17,438
Let me think about it, okay?

309
00:15:17,521 --> 00:15:18,522
[Hocheol exhales sharply]

310
00:15:18,606 --> 00:15:19,815
There's no time for thinking.

311
00:15:20,983 --> 00:15:22,860
I gotta do this before
the chairman returns.

312
00:15:22,944 --> 00:15:24,695
And when is that?

313
00:15:25,738 --> 00:15:27,782
At the end of the month.

314
00:15:27,865 --> 00:15:29,200
I am curious, though.

315
00:15:29,909 --> 00:15:30,952
What's in the casket?

316
00:15:31,577 --> 00:15:32,662
Do you know?

317
00:15:32,745 --> 00:15:35,665
[Jinman] Drugs? Meth?

318
00:15:36,499 --> 00:15:37,833
Organs?

319
00:15:37,917 --> 00:15:41,045
Ah, you gangster assholes keep getting
into organ trafficking these days.

320
00:15:41,128 --> 00:15:42,129
You just can't help yourselves.

321
00:15:42,213 --> 00:15:43,923
[Hocheol] Why the fuck do you need
to know everything?

322
00:15:45,174 --> 00:15:46,550
Just do what you usually do.

323
00:15:47,510 --> 00:15:49,262
Do what I'm telling you.

324
00:15:53,391 --> 00:15:54,976
Ah, hold on.

325
00:15:57,937 --> 00:16:01,983
Do I look like the kind of guy who
just does whatever you tell him to?

326
00:16:04,360 --> 00:16:05,903
Of course I'm that guy.

327
00:16:06,821 --> 00:16:07,822
[Jinman] Right.

328
00:16:07,905 --> 00:16:09,490
[Hocheol scoffs]

329
00:16:09,573 --> 00:16:11,575
[Jinman] Fine, fine, I'll do it.

330
00:16:11,659 --> 00:16:12,660
Huh?

331
00:16:15,454 --> 00:16:17,957
Ah, dammit.
STYLE
::cue()

332
00:16:18,040 --> 00:16:20,960
GANGWON CENTRAL POLICE AGENCY

333
00:16:21,043 --> 00:16:22,753
[distant sirens blaring]

334
00:16:26,674 --> 00:16:29,343
[car door opens]
Oh. Oh, there you are.

335
00:16:29,427 --> 00:16:30,886
[grunting]

336
00:16:30,970 --> 00:16:32,763
-Here.
-Yeah.

337
00:16:34,515 --> 00:16:35,975
[coughs]

338
00:16:39,103 --> 00:16:40,521
Read it, then shred it.

339
00:16:40,604 --> 00:16:43,065
You leave that lying around,
you'll get audited or somethin'.

340
00:16:43,149 --> 00:16:47,111
Oh. You think you're all that just 'cause
you're stationed at headquarters now?

341
00:16:48,821 --> 00:16:50,114
I'm your senior.

342
00:16:51,198 --> 00:16:52,158
ON-SITE INVESTIGATION REPORT

343
00:16:52,241 --> 00:16:53,242
[Detective Kang] It's a burner car.

344
00:16:53,326 --> 00:16:54,660
The plate number is fake, too.

345
00:16:54,744 --> 00:16:56,120
Dash cam?

346
00:16:56,203 --> 00:16:57,204
Nothin'.

347
00:16:57,288 --> 00:16:58,998
No surveillance cams in the area, either.

348
00:16:59,081 --> 00:17:00,458
So we don't know who the driver is.

349
00:17:01,834 --> 00:17:02,835
Why?

350
00:17:03,836 --> 00:17:05,087
The casket?

351
00:17:05,171 --> 00:17:06,589
Those Geumseong guys didn't take it?

352
00:17:06,672 --> 00:17:08,299
I don't think so.

353
00:17:08,382 --> 00:17:09,633
What does that mean?

354
00:17:09,717 --> 00:17:10,968
They either took it or they didn't.

355
00:17:11,052 --> 00:17:12,928
So why do you need all this?

356
00:17:14,096 --> 00:17:16,182
To keep Lee Dokyung quiet
in case he wants to talk?

357
00:17:16,891 --> 00:17:19,602
-Maybe.
-Uh, wait a minute.

358
00:17:20,186 --> 00:17:22,188
I'm not gonna be party to a murder.

359
00:17:22,271 --> 00:17:24,023
If that's the plan then I'm done.

360
00:17:24,106 --> 00:17:25,649
This is the last time I'm helping.

361
00:17:25,733 --> 00:17:27,985
You can tell Park
I'm not doing this anymore.

362
00:17:28,069 --> 00:17:31,197
And doing this will pay off my debts.

363
00:17:31,280 --> 00:17:33,783
[distant sirens wailing]

364
00:17:33,866 --> 00:17:34,867
Hey.

365
00:17:36,202 --> 00:17:37,828
How big of a hole are you in?

366
00:17:37,912 --> 00:17:39,789
100 million won?

367
00:17:40,748 --> 00:17:44,085
Oh, man, you really poured it down
the drain, didn't you?

368
00:17:44,168 --> 00:17:45,169
[groans]

369
00:17:46,003 --> 00:17:48,881
What do you like to play?
Baccarat?

370
00:17:49,799 --> 00:17:52,009
Ah, it won't be easy
to climb outta that hole.

371
00:17:54,762 --> 00:17:55,805
What about you?

372
00:17:56,430 --> 00:17:58,224
How much debt did you end up with?

373
00:17:58,307 --> 00:17:59,850
10 billion won?

374
00:18:01,018 --> 00:18:03,145
That's why you're still in this.
Ever since you were a patrol cop,

375
00:18:03,229 --> 00:18:05,106
you've been cleaning up shit
that Geumseong leaves for you, right?

376
00:18:05,189 --> 00:18:07,149
I paid them all back already.

377
00:18:07,775 --> 00:18:09,276
[Detective Kang] Oh, is that so?

378
00:18:09,360 --> 00:18:12,154
Well, if you're debt free then cleaning
up shit must be in your nature.

379
00:18:12,238 --> 00:18:13,698
[pages flip]

380
00:18:15,199 --> 00:18:17,034
-[Detective Kang exhales]
-You know what?

381
00:18:19,870 --> 00:18:21,622
You're a little shit.

382
00:18:21,706 --> 00:18:23,207
Better watch your mouth.

383
00:18:25,459 --> 00:18:26,794
Actually...

384
00:18:28,796 --> 00:18:29,964
My wife is very sick.

385
00:18:32,925 --> 00:18:34,176
That so?

386
00:18:36,011 --> 00:18:37,179
[Detective Kang exhales]

387
00:18:37,263 --> 00:18:39,849
I'm going.
I don't want to see you again.

388
00:18:39,932 --> 00:18:41,851
Hey, hey, hey.

389
00:18:41,934 --> 00:18:45,354
At least tell me what's
in there before you go. Yeah?

390
00:18:45,438 --> 00:18:46,814
Whatever the hell it is,

391
00:18:46,897 --> 00:18:49,316
it's making the guys
at headquarters crazy.

392
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:51,235
And yet Narcotics are being awfully quiet.

393
00:18:51,318 --> 00:18:52,778
So I guess it's not drugs.

394
00:18:52,862 --> 00:18:54,822
Park didn't tell you anything?

395
00:18:57,241 --> 00:18:58,492
Maybe he doesn't know.

396
00:18:58,576 --> 00:19:00,578
Then what is it?
Come on, just tell me.

397
00:19:01,245 --> 00:19:02,413
-Huh?
-[exhales]

398
00:19:03,748 --> 00:19:07,126
We got the information from Interpol
and it's still under review.

399
00:19:07,209 --> 00:19:08,586
You cannot leak this.

400
00:19:08,669 --> 00:19:10,379
All right, all right, prick.

401
00:19:14,341 --> 00:19:15,426
Gold bars.

402
00:19:18,220 --> 00:19:19,263
Gold bars?

403
00:19:21,515 --> 00:19:23,768
[Detective Kang] There's a Cambodian
trading company funded

404
00:19:23,851 --> 00:19:25,561
by the drug cartel, Krom thom.

405
00:19:25,644 --> 00:19:29,356
The word is that the chairman buried
a massive slush fund.

406
00:19:29,440 --> 00:19:31,609
Under the ground.
Like, actually buried it.

407
00:19:32,985 --> 00:19:34,820
-[scoffs]
-Not cash, but gold bars.

408
00:19:34,904 --> 00:19:36,572
Ten tons worth.

409
00:19:36,655 --> 00:19:39,492
[Detective Kang] Somehow all
this information got leaked.

410
00:19:39,575 --> 00:19:41,076
And the government launched
a massive search

411
00:19:41,160 --> 00:19:42,912
and seizure for tax evasion.

412
00:19:42,995 --> 00:19:46,540
So all those gold bars,
they quickly moved them overseas.

413
00:19:46,624 --> 00:19:48,918
One ton of 10-kilogram gold bars
per shipment,

414
00:19:49,001 --> 00:19:51,253
disguised as caskets. However...

415
00:19:52,296 --> 00:19:53,881
...one was found
at the airport in Hong Kong.

416
00:19:54,465 --> 00:19:56,258
And apparently another one is in Korea.

417
00:19:56,342 --> 00:19:58,260
And that's the casket, huh?

418
00:19:58,344 --> 00:20:00,387
-The one with a ton of gold?
-Yeah, probably.

419
00:20:02,431 --> 00:20:03,516
[Detective Kang] And besides,

420
00:20:03,599 --> 00:20:06,435
that's the only casket that's come in
from Cambodia recently.

421
00:20:16,278 --> 00:20:19,281
[crickets chirping]

422
00:20:34,004 --> 00:20:35,047
[tires squeak]

423
00:20:36,340 --> 00:20:37,800
[gears shift]

424
00:20:41,679 --> 00:20:45,140
SEONGOGAE REST AREA
STYLE
::cue()

425
00:20:58,946 --> 00:21:01,782
-Is anybody here?
-[Female Store Owner] Hi, there.

426
00:21:01,866 --> 00:21:03,951
-Yes, hello.
-[Female Store Owner] Ah, yes.

427
00:21:04,034 --> 00:21:07,037
Excuse me,
but the surveillance camera outside,

428
00:21:07,121 --> 00:21:08,289
did you install it?

429
00:21:09,039 --> 00:21:10,499
[Female Store Owner] Yes.

430
00:21:10,583 --> 00:21:12,209
Well, I'm with the police. Here.

431
00:21:12,293 --> 00:21:13,627
I'm Detective Kim Jinman.

432
00:21:13,711 --> 00:21:16,964
I reported the installation of that camera
to the police already.

433
00:21:17,047 --> 00:21:18,257
Might there be an issue?

434
00:21:18,340 --> 00:21:20,134
Oh, no, no.
It's nothing like that.

435
00:21:20,217 --> 00:21:22,636
There was a traffic accident out front
a few days ago.

436
00:21:22,720 --> 00:21:24,680
-I just want to check something out. Yeah.
-[Female Store Owner] I see.

437
00:21:25,931 --> 00:21:27,349
[mouse clicking]

438
00:21:27,433 --> 00:21:30,436
[computer hard drive clicking]

439
00:21:33,314 --> 00:21:34,356
[mouse clicks]

440
00:21:35,274 --> 00:21:36,525
GANGWON CENTRAL POLICE AGENCY
TRAFFIC INFORMATION CENTER

441
00:21:36,609 --> 00:21:37,902
-One moment. I'll take a look.
-[Jinman] Yeah.

442
00:21:37,985 --> 00:21:39,862
[clicking]
[Female Police Officer] Okay.

443
00:21:39,945 --> 00:21:43,073
12:29 A.M.
Jingogae Intersection.

444
00:21:43,157 --> 00:21:46,869
And at 12:57 A.M.,
21 Jinbu Street.

445
00:21:46,952 --> 00:21:50,956
Next, at 1:32 A.M.
National Route 59.

446
00:21:51,040 --> 00:21:52,458
[Female Police Officer]
And at 1:55 A.M.,

447
00:21:52,541 --> 00:21:54,126
crossing Jeongsan Bridge.

448
00:21:55,044 --> 00:21:56,128
Jeongsan?

449
00:21:57,212 --> 00:21:58,422
[Female Police Officer] Yes.

450
00:21:59,506 --> 00:22:00,966
GEUMSEONG TOURIST HOTEL

451
00:22:01,050 --> 00:22:06,722
[All] ♪ I'm begging you please
Don't cling to me anymore ♪

452
00:22:06,805 --> 00:22:08,390
[Jinman] ♪ Don't come looking for me ♪

453
00:22:08,474 --> 00:22:09,725
Stop it.

454
00:22:09,808 --> 00:22:12,603
Ah, honey, it's fine.

455
00:22:12,686 --> 00:22:14,980
Wow, what's up with your hands?

456
00:22:15,064 --> 00:22:16,523
They're so pretty for a man.

457
00:22:16,607 --> 00:22:18,108
Because they're woman's hands.

458
00:22:18,192 --> 00:22:20,027
That means it's fine if I touch you,
right?

459
00:22:20,110 --> 00:22:21,570
[Jinman] Just kidding!

460
00:22:21,654 --> 00:22:25,491
♪ A heartless girl
when I'm already breaking inside ♪

461
00:22:25,574 --> 00:22:27,034
Park Hocheol's here!

462
00:22:27,117 --> 00:22:28,953
♪ So now just for a while... ♪

463
00:22:29,036 --> 00:22:29,954
CANCEL

464
00:22:30,037 --> 00:22:31,038
-[Jinman] Hey.
-What?

465
00:22:31,121 --> 00:22:32,665
-I finally found my love today!
-Get him outta here.

466
00:22:32,748 --> 00:22:34,375
-It's no fair!
-I know, I know.

467
00:22:34,458 --> 00:22:35,709
-[Jinman] Oh, honey.
-[laughing]

468
00:22:35,793 --> 00:22:38,420
[Jinman] You know, right?
My love?

469
00:22:38,504 --> 00:22:40,923
Honey, I have to be really honest
with you.

470
00:22:41,006 --> 00:22:42,591
Jeongah.

471
00:22:42,675 --> 00:22:43,884
Sorry!

472
00:22:44,760 --> 00:22:46,345
Oh, look.
Park has arrived.

473
00:22:46,428 --> 00:22:48,764
[Jinman] Right when we're getting
this party started.

474
00:22:48,847 --> 00:22:50,057
[door closes]

475
00:22:50,140 --> 00:22:52,309
I'm taking two of those girls out with me.

476
00:22:52,393 --> 00:22:55,104
-Have you found anything?
-[Jinman] Of course I did!

477
00:22:55,187 --> 00:22:56,689
Wait, what did I...

478
00:22:57,606 --> 00:22:59,108
You talkin' about the van?

479
00:22:59,775 --> 00:23:01,735
Yeah, I've been looking around for it.

480
00:23:01,819 --> 00:23:04,196
I combed through the surveillance cameras
in Gangwon-do.

481
00:23:04,279 --> 00:23:05,614
I checked every single one.

482
00:23:05,698 --> 00:23:07,241
Quit rambling and just spit it out.

483
00:23:08,826 --> 00:23:09,827
Hey.

484
00:23:09,910 --> 00:23:11,996
[Jinman] I'm taking two of them today.

485
00:23:12,538 --> 00:23:14,123
-Yes, sir.
-[Jinman] Yeah? You got it?

486
00:23:14,206 --> 00:23:15,249
-[Jinman] Huh?
-[Hocheol] Hey.

487
00:23:15,332 --> 00:23:16,834
-Move it.
-[Jinman] Yeah.

488
00:23:16,917 --> 00:23:18,711
Yeah, go get-
what are you doing?

489
00:23:18,794 --> 00:23:21,130
[Jinman] Go. Get them ready.
Good.

490
00:23:22,464 --> 00:23:23,882
Ah.

491
00:23:23,966 --> 00:23:25,551
[Jinman] What was I saying?

492
00:23:26,719 --> 00:23:28,178
[Jinman] Oh, right. The van.

493
00:23:29,096 --> 00:23:33,392
Was last seen here in Jeongsan.
Where we are.

494
00:23:33,475 --> 00:23:36,228
[Jinman] It was caught
on surveillance cameras.

495
00:23:36,311 --> 00:23:39,565
It shows up at the entrance
to Jeongsan Bridge.

496
00:23:39,648 --> 00:23:41,066
[Jinman] Then no trace of it anywhere.

497
00:23:41,150 --> 00:23:42,526
And two days later,

498
00:23:42,609 --> 00:23:45,738
they dump the van
at the abandoned warehouse,

499
00:23:45,821 --> 00:23:47,281
but it was empty.

500
00:23:48,032 --> 00:23:50,909
[Jinman] So where did they hide
the casket? Huh?

501
00:23:50,993 --> 00:23:52,411
[Hocheol exhales]

502
00:23:52,494 --> 00:23:54,246
[clacks on table]
Right here.

503
00:23:54,329 --> 00:23:55,873
Jeongsan.

504
00:23:55,956 --> 00:23:58,083
They hid it here.

505
00:23:58,167 --> 00:24:00,753
So who was it, then?
The prick who was driving it?

506
00:24:00,836 --> 00:24:02,629
Oh, I don't really know about that.

507
00:24:02,713 --> 00:24:06,592
But either way, I've really
helped you narrow it down.

508
00:24:06,675 --> 00:24:09,803
Just find out who was in Jeongsan that day
and catch 'em.

509
00:24:10,804 --> 00:24:11,805
[Jinman] Wouldn't that work?

510
00:24:11,889 --> 00:24:12,890
Find out quickly.

511
00:24:14,683 --> 00:24:17,519
Right, but I think I got a hold
of some info that you're gonna wanna hear.

512
00:24:18,312 --> 00:24:19,980
Yeah. You should know.

513
00:24:20,064 --> 00:24:21,982
-[Jinman] Yeah?
-What?

514
00:24:22,066 --> 00:24:24,985
I'm guessing you don't know what's in
that casket, do you?

515
00:24:25,069 --> 00:24:26,111
[Jinman] Well?

516
00:24:29,198 --> 00:24:31,658
You don't know, huh?
Well, I do.

517
00:24:32,868 --> 00:24:34,620
[inhales sharply]

518
00:24:36,330 --> 00:24:37,873
What's in it?

519
00:24:37,956 --> 00:24:41,043
Well, this info's worth
at least 100 gold chips.

520
00:24:41,126 --> 00:24:42,711
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
We can do that.

521
00:24:44,922 --> 00:24:46,757
Gold bars.

522
00:24:48,759 --> 00:24:50,385
[Jinman] A ton of them.

523
00:24:51,220 --> 00:24:52,554
[Jinman] One ton.

524
00:24:53,472 --> 00:24:54,723
The current market value...

525
00:24:56,350 --> 00:24:57,726
150 billion.

526
00:24:57,810 --> 00:24:59,603
[Jinman] Crazy, right?

527
00:25:00,687 --> 00:25:03,482
[Jinman] But then again,
you know what's really crazy?

528
00:25:03,565 --> 00:25:09,404
Is that, well, the chairman didn't
tell you you'd be smuggling gold, huh?

529
00:25:09,488 --> 00:25:10,906
Why is that?

530
00:25:11,657 --> 00:25:14,034
Seems like the kind of important stuff
you should know.

531
00:25:16,411 --> 00:25:18,997
[Jinman] I mean,
you are his right-hand man.

532
00:25:19,081 --> 00:25:20,791
[Jinman] Does that mean...

533
00:25:20,874 --> 00:25:22,709
...is he demoting you?

534
00:25:24,461 --> 00:25:26,505
[Jinman] Guess it doesn't matter.

535
00:25:27,256 --> 00:25:28,715
[Jinman] As long as you get the job done.
STYLE
::cue()

536
00:25:34,388 --> 00:25:36,515
Yeah. So.

537
00:25:36,598 --> 00:25:39,143
I heard that you're one
of the best goldsmiths in the area.

538
00:25:40,185 --> 00:25:43,272
Uh, yes, well...

539
00:25:43,355 --> 00:25:45,732
-You've manufactured gold bars yourself?
-[Hoonseok] Yes.

540
00:25:45,816 --> 00:25:48,152
[Woogy] I need you to make ten bars.

541
00:25:48,235 --> 00:25:50,404
One kilo each, just like
I said on the phone.

542
00:25:50,487 --> 00:25:52,156
And of course we'll provide the gold.

543
00:25:53,198 --> 00:25:54,324
[Woogy] And your casting fee?

544
00:25:54,408 --> 00:25:55,534
Mm...

545
00:25:57,703 --> 00:25:58,912
One percent of cost.

546
00:25:58,996 --> 00:26:00,998
[Woogy] Pretty good, right?

547
00:26:01,081 --> 00:26:03,250
It's not every day you get
an offer like this.

548
00:26:04,501 --> 00:26:06,962
[Woogy] I'm curious,
how long will it take to make them?

549
00:26:07,921 --> 00:26:09,548
Around two to three days.

550
00:26:09,631 --> 00:26:11,341
-Two to three.
-[Hoonseok] You see,

551
00:26:11,425 --> 00:26:12,301
gold bars don't require...

552
00:26:12,384 --> 00:26:13,844
[shushes]

553
00:26:15,053 --> 00:26:16,763
Detailed craftsmanship.

554
00:26:17,347 --> 00:26:18,348
One thing, though.

555
00:26:18,432 --> 00:26:20,893
Where in Jeongsan are you from, exactly?

556
00:26:21,810 --> 00:26:23,812
[Hoonseok] Don't you have a business card?

557
00:26:23,896 --> 00:26:25,689
It's just that normally gold bars

558
00:26:25,772 --> 00:26:28,567
are manufactured
in specific authorized factories,

559
00:26:28,650 --> 00:26:29,860
so why don't you go to those?

560
00:26:29,943 --> 00:26:31,403
The thing is...

561
00:26:32,905 --> 00:26:34,948
There's a reason why I'm paying you such
a high fee.

562
00:26:36,325 --> 00:26:37,659
It comes with one condition.

563
00:26:38,702 --> 00:26:39,912
What condition, you ask?

564
00:26:39,995 --> 00:26:41,413
No questions.

565
00:26:41,496 --> 00:26:44,791
[Woogy] The who, what, why, where,
none of it.

566
00:26:44,875 --> 00:26:46,919
They say silence is golden, right?

567
00:26:47,002 --> 00:26:50,923
[Woogy] So stay silent
and you can call it a golden fee.

568
00:26:51,006 --> 00:26:52,633
A golden fee?

569
00:26:52,716 --> 00:26:53,967
[Woogy] Yeah, that's right.

570
00:26:54,051 --> 00:26:55,802
And there's a second condition.

571
00:26:55,886 --> 00:26:57,179
It's not just questions.

572
00:26:57,262 --> 00:26:58,764
You can't say anything.

573
00:26:58,847 --> 00:26:59,848
[Woogy] You can't go around saying,

574
00:26:59,932 --> 00:27:02,601
"Hey, I'm working on this gold job.
They're 10-kilo bars,"

575
00:27:02,684 --> 00:27:04,561
to literally anyone.
If you do,

576
00:27:04,645 --> 00:27:06,146
our contract is over.

577
00:27:06,230 --> 00:27:08,941
[Woogy] Not only that,
your life will be over.

578
00:27:09,024 --> 00:27:10,359
Then you bought them illegally.

579
00:27:11,360 --> 00:27:12,653
[Hoonseok] If I refuse now...

580
00:27:13,570 --> 00:27:15,030
...I'll be okay, right?

581
00:27:18,200 --> 00:27:19,493
Of course.

582
00:27:19,576 --> 00:27:23,497
Mm, it's not like you saw
the gold or anything.

583
00:27:23,580 --> 00:27:25,165
So yeah,
if you don't wanna do it,

584
00:27:25,248 --> 00:27:27,376
no biggie.
It's not like anyone saw us here.

585
00:27:27,459 --> 00:27:31,880
No one knows that we met to talk and-
two percent, okay?

586
00:27:33,382 --> 00:27:34,591
3K per kilo.

587
00:27:35,467 --> 00:27:37,552
300 million for ten bars.

588
00:27:37,636 --> 00:27:39,137
[Woogy] Do you know anyone
who makes that in a month?

589
00:27:40,055 --> 00:27:42,349
I wouldn't offer this to anybody else,
Hoonseok.

590
00:27:42,432 --> 00:27:44,309
I like your face.

591
00:27:44,393 --> 00:27:47,562
[Woogy] You look like the type of guy
who'd make gold bars with total precision.

592
00:27:47,646 --> 00:27:49,231
I really want to work with you, okay?

593
00:27:51,316 --> 00:27:52,901
But if you'd rather refuse, say so, hmm?

594
00:27:52,985 --> 00:27:54,945
I'm a busy man.
I have to go look for someone else now.

595
00:27:55,028 --> 00:27:57,698
-We're done here.
-[Hoonseok] The gold bar.

596
00:27:58,740 --> 00:28:01,201
Show me.
Then I'll decide.

597
00:28:03,453 --> 00:28:04,454
Okay.

598
00:28:10,043 --> 00:28:12,671
Here. This is it.

599
00:28:12,754 --> 00:28:13,880
[Hoonseok] Okay.

600
00:28:21,346 --> 00:28:22,931
[Woogy sniffs]
Here he is.

601
00:28:23,015 --> 00:28:24,391
Mr. Lee Hoonseok.

602
00:28:25,892 --> 00:28:27,144
Yeah.

603
00:28:27,227 --> 00:28:29,021
And this is, uh...

604
00:28:30,147 --> 00:28:31,231
Call her Boss.

605
00:28:32,649 --> 00:28:35,068
Nice to meet you, Boss.

606
00:28:36,194 --> 00:28:37,571
Hello.

607
00:28:37,988 --> 00:28:39,239
[Woogy] He's going to work with us.

608
00:28:39,322 --> 00:28:40,657
He'll make the...

609
00:28:42,659 --> 00:28:44,411
You know what?
I've noticed your voice is kind of loud,

610
00:28:44,494 --> 00:28:46,580
so from now on we'll call
the gold bars "potatoes," okay?

611
00:28:47,330 --> 00:28:48,415
Show him the potato.

612
00:28:49,666 --> 00:28:51,334
[Woogy] He wants to check it.
STYLE
::cue()

613
00:28:54,880 --> 00:28:56,423
Hey, it's okay.
You're good to show him.

614
00:28:58,133 --> 00:28:59,760
[Woogy] We're all in the same boat now
so it's cool.

615
00:29:01,136 --> 00:29:03,055
[bag rustling and unzipping]

616
00:29:04,723 --> 00:29:06,349
[Heeju grunts]

617
00:29:06,433 --> 00:29:09,728
[both grunting]

618
00:29:09,811 --> 00:29:11,354
Here.

619
00:29:11,438 --> 00:29:12,981
[Woogy grunts]

620
00:29:13,065 --> 00:29:14,149
[exhales sharply]

621
00:29:17,611 --> 00:29:20,197
[scraping]

622
00:29:32,834 --> 00:29:34,628
This is real.

623
00:29:36,004 --> 00:29:38,006
Well, of course it is.
It's the real deal.

624
00:29:40,258 --> 00:29:41,760
All right, I'll have it done.

625
00:29:41,843 --> 00:29:43,553
It won't take long.
Come back tomorrow night.

626
00:29:43,637 --> 00:29:45,138
Uh, no, no, no.

627
00:29:46,598 --> 00:29:47,599
It'd be better...

628
00:29:47,682 --> 00:29:49,684
[grunts]

629
00:29:49,768 --> 00:29:50,936
[Heeju] ...if you could start work today.

630
00:29:51,019 --> 00:29:52,521
-[Heeju] And I would like to supervise.
-[grunts]

631
00:29:52,604 --> 00:29:55,398
That's right. And while she's watching,
I'll also be watching.

632
00:29:56,942 --> 00:29:58,485
I can't do it right away.

633
00:29:58,568 --> 00:30:01,321
I need to get things like
a new crucible and new molds,

634
00:30:01,404 --> 00:30:02,823
and if we're stamping
the Korea Mint mark...

635
00:30:02,906 --> 00:30:03,949
I can wait.

636
00:30:04,866 --> 00:30:06,576
[Woogy] Yeah, yeah.
We can wait.

637
00:30:06,660 --> 00:30:09,121
Hey, you can understand
why she's suspicious.

638
00:30:09,204 --> 00:30:11,081
You can get all those things today, right?

639
00:30:11,164 --> 00:30:13,208
Then we can get started tonight, huh?

640
00:30:13,291 --> 00:30:14,417
Pull an all-nighter?

641
00:30:16,753 --> 00:30:18,088
How about this?

642
00:30:19,339 --> 00:30:20,465
Midnight tonight.

643
00:30:21,383 --> 00:30:22,968
Come to the front of the workshop.

644
00:30:24,928 --> 00:30:26,388
When everything's all set,
I'll give you guys a call.

645
00:30:26,471 --> 00:30:27,848
-And I'll let you inside.
-[Woogy] Nice.

646
00:30:27,931 --> 00:30:29,141
[Heeju] All right.

647
00:30:29,224 --> 00:30:30,225
So I'll call you later.

648
00:30:32,018 --> 00:30:33,728
-See you at midnight.
-Mm-hmm.

649
00:30:33,812 --> 00:30:35,772
Call us. Call us later.

650
00:30:36,481 --> 00:30:37,482
[car door closes]

651
00:30:39,067 --> 00:30:40,610
[exhales sharply]

652
00:30:41,778 --> 00:30:42,988
[Woogy] See?

653
00:30:43,071 --> 00:30:44,406
What'd I say?

654
00:30:44,489 --> 00:30:46,116
There's nothing money can't buy.

655
00:30:46,199 --> 00:30:49,286
Do you really think he's the right guy?

656
00:30:49,369 --> 00:30:50,704
He seems too nice.

657
00:30:51,997 --> 00:30:53,248
So? What's wrong with being a nice guy?

658
00:30:53,331 --> 00:30:54,583
[Heeju] He could have a sudden change
of heart

659
00:30:54,666 --> 00:30:57,627
and decide to report us to the police.

660
00:30:57,711 --> 00:30:59,171
Stop worrying about that.

661
00:30:59,254 --> 00:31:01,131
I told you I did
a background check on the guy.

662
00:31:02,048 --> 00:31:03,383
That guy there?

663
00:31:04,301 --> 00:31:06,303
He lives with his widowed mother
and sister.

664
00:31:06,386 --> 00:31:08,263
He's the breadwinner of the family.

665
00:31:08,346 --> 00:31:09,598
So what?

666
00:31:10,724 --> 00:31:12,058
[exhales sharply]
Heeju.

667
00:31:12,893 --> 00:31:15,228
This is how we make deals in my world,
okay?

668
00:31:15,312 --> 00:31:17,230
Money's important
but collateral's necessary.

669
00:31:17,314 --> 00:31:18,607
It's absolutely essential.

670
00:31:18,690 --> 00:31:21,151
Last thing you want
is to get stabbed in the back.

671
00:31:21,234 --> 00:31:23,486
So you always have to consider
the worst-case scenario.

672
00:31:23,570 --> 00:31:24,988
And these guys?

673
00:31:25,071 --> 00:31:28,033
What's the one thing that keeps them
from doing something stupid or crazy?

674
00:31:28,116 --> 00:31:29,868
Collateral, of course.

675
00:31:29,951 --> 00:31:31,494
The more important the collateral is,

676
00:31:31,578 --> 00:31:33,288
the less likely they are
to screw us over.

677
00:31:34,748 --> 00:31:35,999
So you're saying...

678
00:31:37,167 --> 00:31:40,503
...his mom and younger sister
are collateral?

679
00:31:43,215 --> 00:31:45,926
-Ah, come on. You know what I mean.
-[Heeju] Then what's my collateral?

680
00:31:46,009 --> 00:31:47,469
Is it my aunt?

681
00:31:49,554 --> 00:31:50,555
Heeju.

682
00:31:50,639 --> 00:31:52,015
That's why you went to the pawn shop
the other day.

683
00:31:52,098 --> 00:31:53,475
To check on my collateral?

684
00:31:53,558 --> 00:31:55,227
Are you seriously asking me that?

685
00:31:55,310 --> 00:31:56,895
I went because I wanted to see Auntie.

686
00:31:56,978 --> 00:31:59,689
You got it all wrong.
It's not like that.

687
00:31:59,773 --> 00:32:01,066
Ah, come on.

688
00:32:01,149 --> 00:32:02,442
Collateral's insane.

689
00:32:02,525 --> 00:32:04,569
How 'bout we go eat?
What do you want?

690
00:32:04,653 --> 00:32:06,029
[grunts]

691
00:32:06,112 --> 00:32:07,364
Bokjiri sounds good..
STYLE
::cue()

692
00:32:10,033 --> 00:32:13,119
[crickets chirping]

693
00:32:13,203 --> 00:32:14,454
[Heeju] Something's wrong.

694
00:32:15,747 --> 00:32:16,915
Give him a call.

695
00:32:16,998 --> 00:32:18,291
[Woogy] Well, he said he'd call
when he's ready.

696
00:32:18,375 --> 00:32:19,668
[cell phone vibrates]

697
00:32:23,421 --> 00:32:24,422
Yeah?

698
00:32:25,799 --> 00:32:26,841
Mm, okay.

699
00:32:28,969 --> 00:32:30,220
[Woogy grunting]

700
00:32:31,388 --> 00:32:34,224
[breathing heavily]

701
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:02,585
JEIL WORKSHOP

702
00:33:02,669 --> 00:33:04,170
[keypad beeping]

703
00:33:05,630 --> 00:33:06,881
[door locks unlocking]

704
00:33:06,965 --> 00:33:08,216
[door squeaks]

705
00:33:08,300 --> 00:33:09,509
[light switches click]

706
00:33:09,592 --> 00:33:12,304
[whirring]

707
00:33:17,809 --> 00:33:19,936
[door locks beeping]

708
00:33:21,980 --> 00:33:23,315
Oh, here.

709
00:33:23,398 --> 00:33:24,524
Oh.

710
00:33:33,033 --> 00:33:34,868
[Woogy] I got it.

711
00:33:34,951 --> 00:33:36,119
Here.

712
00:33:36,202 --> 00:33:38,079
[both grunting]

713
00:33:38,163 --> 00:33:39,247
[gold bar thuds]

714
00:33:39,331 --> 00:33:41,291
[zipper unzips]

715
00:33:43,376 --> 00:33:44,919
How long will it take?

716
00:33:45,003 --> 00:33:47,505
I'll be done with it before morning.

717
00:33:47,589 --> 00:33:50,383
I guess you two just wait here.

718
00:33:52,218 --> 00:33:55,221
Yeah, and don't you even think
about pulling any stunts.

719
00:33:55,305 --> 00:33:57,098
I'll be watching you.

720
00:33:58,224 --> 00:33:59,976
[Woogy] I'm watching you over there, too!

721
00:34:00,060 --> 00:34:03,480
[scraping]

722
00:34:05,982 --> 00:34:07,442
[exhales sharply]

723
00:34:07,525 --> 00:34:08,902
[heat hissing]

724
00:34:08,985 --> 00:34:10,445
[exhales]

725
00:34:12,072 --> 00:34:13,907
[bar clinking]

726
00:34:16,117 --> 00:34:17,077
[hissing]

727
00:34:17,160 --> 00:34:18,244
[door clangs]

728
00:34:23,750 --> 00:34:25,543
[fire roars]

729
00:34:30,715 --> 00:34:33,718
[flames hissing]

730
00:34:43,770 --> 00:34:46,773
[melted gold splatting]

731
00:34:50,235 --> 00:34:53,279
[flames hiss]

732
00:34:54,364 --> 00:34:55,949
[gold clinks]

733
00:34:57,033 --> 00:34:58,910
[water sizzling]

734
00:35:03,248 --> 00:35:04,916
[bars clink]

735
00:35:04,999 --> 00:35:07,961
[flames roaring]

736
00:35:08,044 --> 00:35:10,046
[cell phone vibrating]

737
00:35:10,130 --> 00:35:13,675
INCOMING CALL
JEIL WORKSHOP PRESIDENT NOH

738
00:35:13,758 --> 00:35:16,761
JEWELRY ECONOMY DAILY

739
00:35:16,845 --> 00:35:19,472
[distant gold clinking]

740
00:35:19,556 --> 00:35:20,682
[exhales]

741
00:35:21,433 --> 00:35:22,559
That's right.

742
00:35:27,731 --> 00:35:29,858
You went into that coal mine.

743
00:35:30,775 --> 00:35:32,944
[distant thunder rumbling]

744
00:35:33,027 --> 00:35:34,487
[thunder cracks]

745
00:35:34,571 --> 00:35:36,030
DAD! BE SAFE AGAIN TODAY

746
00:35:48,918 --> 00:35:50,128
You were there?

747
00:35:51,087 --> 00:35:53,757
Of course I was.

748
00:35:55,633 --> 00:35:57,051
[exhales]

749
00:35:57,135 --> 00:35:59,429
[inhales and exhales sharply]

750
00:36:00,513 --> 00:36:01,639
What was the name of that mutt, again?

751
00:36:03,099 --> 00:36:04,851
[Woogy] Mongsil or something.

752
00:36:06,060 --> 00:36:07,353
Don't you remember?

753
00:36:07,437 --> 00:36:09,230
You went in there while we
were playing freeze tag, I think.

754
00:36:11,316 --> 00:36:12,942
[Woogy] You were looking
for that stupid dog

755
00:36:13,026 --> 00:36:14,694
and I waited for you forever.

756
00:36:14,778 --> 00:36:16,070
[newspaper page turns]

757
00:36:16,154 --> 00:36:18,448
I kept waiting,
but you didn't come out.

758
00:36:18,531 --> 00:36:20,867
So I went to get the Aunties.

759
00:36:23,119 --> 00:36:25,121
[9-Year-Old Heeju] Mongsil, wait!
STYLE
::cue()

760
00:36:25,205 --> 00:36:26,998
[dog yaps]

761
00:36:27,081 --> 00:36:28,541
[9-Year-Old Heeju] Mongsil!

762
00:36:29,959 --> 00:36:31,044
[distant dog yaps]

763
00:36:33,046 --> 00:36:34,297
Mongsil!

764
00:36:37,133 --> 00:36:38,968
Mongsil, here!

765
00:36:48,311 --> 00:36:49,646
[9-Year-Old Heeju] Mongsil!

766
00:36:52,774 --> 00:36:53,983
Heeju.

767
00:36:56,319 --> 00:36:57,403
[Woogy] You don't remember?

768
00:36:58,321 --> 00:36:59,531
[exhales]

769
00:37:00,573 --> 00:37:03,576
I'm not sure.
I don't think so.

770
00:37:05,662 --> 00:37:07,372
You really forgot.

771
00:37:08,456 --> 00:37:10,708
[Woogy] Come on.
You gotta remember.

772
00:37:10,792 --> 00:37:13,002
I practically saved your life, you know?

773
00:37:13,878 --> 00:37:14,879
[Heeju] I don't know.

774
00:37:14,963 --> 00:37:16,464
[Heeju] I seriously don't remember.

775
00:37:17,966 --> 00:37:19,384
[Woogy exhales sharply]

776
00:37:21,135 --> 00:37:22,136
[sighs]

777
00:37:23,429 --> 00:37:26,933
[cell phone vibrating]

778
00:37:43,491 --> 00:37:46,035
[door lock beeping]

779
00:37:47,078 --> 00:37:48,997
[chiming]

780
00:37:49,080 --> 00:37:50,498
[door handle rattles]

781
00:37:50,582 --> 00:37:52,333
Hoonseok?

782
00:37:52,417 --> 00:37:54,210
[gasps and shushes]

783
00:37:54,294 --> 00:37:56,629
-[Hoonseok] Shh, quiet. Quiet.
-[President Noh] Are you there?

784
00:37:57,463 --> 00:37:58,464
Who is it?

785
00:37:59,841 --> 00:38:01,259
[Woogy] Hey! What are you doing?

786
00:38:01,342 --> 00:38:03,845
It's-it's the owner.

787
00:38:03,928 --> 00:38:05,555
[all gasping]

788
00:38:05,638 --> 00:38:06,806
Hold on.

789
00:38:08,433 --> 00:38:09,893
[gold clinking]

790
00:38:09,976 --> 00:38:11,311
Hoonseok!

791
00:38:13,187 --> 00:38:14,397
Quick, come on.

792
00:38:14,480 --> 00:38:15,899
-Come on.
-[President Noh] Are you asleep?

793
00:38:15,982 --> 00:38:17,191
[gasps]

794
00:38:20,612 --> 00:38:22,238
[President Noh] Hoonseok.

795
00:38:22,322 --> 00:38:24,449
[locks clacking]

796
00:38:25,575 --> 00:38:26,868
Ah, goodness.

797
00:38:26,951 --> 00:38:29,078
So you were in here.

798
00:38:29,162 --> 00:38:30,496
Yes. What are you...

799
00:38:30,580 --> 00:38:32,624
Well, why did you lock the door?

800
00:38:32,707 --> 00:38:34,584
What are you doing up at this hour?

801
00:38:37,045 --> 00:38:38,713
Uh, sir, can I talk to you for a sec?

802
00:38:40,715 --> 00:38:41,716
Hold on.

803
00:38:44,218 --> 00:38:47,138
[Hoonseok] There's nothing...

804
00:38:48,723 --> 00:38:49,766
[Hoonseok] Sir?

805
00:38:52,101 --> 00:38:53,770
Wait.

806
00:38:53,853 --> 00:38:55,855
What-what's all that?

807
00:38:58,900 --> 00:39:01,069
-[nervous exhale]
-[President Noh] Spit it out!

808
00:39:01,152 --> 00:39:02,445
[President Noh] What are you up to?

809
00:39:03,446 --> 00:39:05,907
[Hoonseok] Someone from Janggak asked me
to do some craft work.

810
00:39:05,990 --> 00:39:07,367
Let go.

811
00:39:07,450 --> 00:39:08,451
[both grunting]

812
00:39:08,534 --> 00:39:10,787
[President Noh] What? Seems like a lot.

813
00:39:10,870 --> 00:39:13,706
[Hoonseok] It's 14k.
There's not much gold in it.

814
00:39:15,083 --> 00:39:16,250
[Hoonseok] Hold on, sir!

815
00:39:16,334 --> 00:39:17,210
Why do you wanna go in there?

816
00:39:17,293 --> 00:39:19,504
[Hoonseok] There's nothing to...

817
00:39:19,587 --> 00:39:20,922
Goodness, what's with you?

818
00:39:21,005 --> 00:39:22,340
[President Noh grunts]

819
00:39:26,469 --> 00:39:28,012
What are you doing at this hour?

820
00:39:28,096 --> 00:39:29,305
Why aren't you at home sleeping?

821
00:39:32,976 --> 00:39:34,310
[President Noh groans]

822
00:39:34,394 --> 00:39:35,812
I couldn't sleep.

823
00:39:35,895 --> 00:39:37,397
[exhales sharply]

824
00:39:39,148 --> 00:39:41,943
I decided to sell this factory
to President Choi.

825
00:39:42,902 --> 00:39:44,320
[President Noh]
It's best you stop working here...

826
00:39:46,072 --> 00:39:47,448
...and look somewhere else.

827
00:39:47,532 --> 00:39:48,700
But sir...

828
00:39:49,701 --> 00:39:51,160
I'm very sorry.

829
00:39:51,869 --> 00:39:53,746
I wanted to help you send your sister
to college.

830
00:39:54,664 --> 00:39:56,749
And of course I wanted to help your mom.

831
00:39:56,833 --> 00:39:59,544
Make sure you could take care
of her while she's unwell.

832
00:40:00,253 --> 00:40:02,922
[President Noh] But there's just
no way I can hold on anymore.

833
00:40:04,924 --> 00:40:06,551
Forget about me.

834
00:40:06,634 --> 00:40:09,262
What are you going
to do about paying off your loan?

835
00:40:09,345 --> 00:40:12,348
I thought you said Mr. Choi's offer
wasn't that great.

836
00:40:12,432 --> 00:40:15,059
[chuckles]
Look, I wasn't good enough.

837
00:40:15,143 --> 00:40:17,186
[President Noh] That's why I'm in debt.
What can you do?

838
00:40:17,270 --> 00:40:18,980
[President Noh exhales sharply]
Okay.

839
00:40:20,481 --> 00:40:21,649
Be careful.

840
00:40:21,733 --> 00:40:24,652
I hear there are a lot
of thieves stealing gold dust.

841
00:40:25,361 --> 00:40:27,113
Better keep the doors locked up.

842
00:40:27,196 --> 00:40:28,448
Yeah.

843
00:40:28,531 --> 00:40:30,366
Thank you.

844
00:40:30,450 --> 00:40:32,827
You've always been a hard worker.

845
00:40:32,910 --> 00:40:33,911
[chuckles]

846
00:40:33,995 --> 00:40:35,163
[exhales]

847
00:40:37,457 --> 00:40:38,458
[relieved exhale]
STYLE
::cue()

848
00:40:42,962 --> 00:40:45,006
[gold bar clatters]
[both gasp]

849
00:40:45,089 --> 00:40:46,090
[clanging]

850
00:40:47,550 --> 00:40:49,218
Wait a minute.
What was that noise?

851
00:40:50,094 --> 00:40:52,388
Uh, what noise?
I didn't hear any noise.

852
00:40:52,472 --> 00:40:54,390
-What's wrong with you?
-[Hoonseok] Nothing.

853
00:40:54,474 --> 00:40:55,475
Get out of my way, kid!

854
00:40:55,558 --> 00:40:57,685
-[President Noh] What was that?
-[Hoonseok] That was nothing!

855
00:40:57,769 --> 00:41:00,063
-[Hoonseok] You should just go...
-I'm going in!

856
00:41:00,146 --> 00:41:02,482
Sir, wait, please!
Don't go in there!

857
00:41:03,858 --> 00:41:04,901
[all shouting]

858
00:41:05,860 --> 00:41:09,572
[blow lands]
[all yelling]

859
00:41:09,655 --> 00:41:11,407
We're fucked.
We're so fucked.

860
00:41:11,491 --> 00:41:12,658
Sir, are you okay?

861
00:41:14,118 --> 00:41:16,204
Why'd you do that?

862
00:41:16,287 --> 00:41:18,790
Sir, are you okay?

863
00:41:20,124 --> 00:41:21,709
[Heeju] He needs to go to the hospital.

864
00:41:23,669 --> 00:41:25,505
[Heeju] We have to take him, okay?

865
00:41:27,340 --> 00:41:29,383
[Heeju] Woogy. Hey. Hey!

866
00:41:29,467 --> 00:41:30,718
What are you doing?

867
00:41:31,552 --> 00:41:32,553
We have no choice.

868
00:41:32,637 --> 00:41:34,097
He saw the gold bar
so I gotta finish him off.

869
00:41:34,180 --> 00:41:35,139
-No!
-[Hoonseok] Are you crazy?

870
00:41:35,223 --> 00:41:36,974
-[both grunting]
-Let go.

871
00:41:37,058 --> 00:41:38,142
Let go!

872
00:41:38,226 --> 00:41:40,311
[Heeju] Wait! Wait a second!

873
00:41:40,394 --> 00:41:42,146
Just-just put that down, okay?

874
00:41:42,230 --> 00:41:43,856
If you don't wanna help,
get out of the way.

875
00:41:44,774 --> 00:41:46,567
-[Woogy] I gotta cut him into pieces.
-No! You can't do that, no!

876
00:41:46,651 --> 00:41:47,860
[Heeju] Cut him up?

877
00:41:47,944 --> 00:41:49,737
-He's alive still!
-[Woogy] Is he?

878
00:41:49,821 --> 00:41:51,614
I guess I just have to kill him, then!

879
00:41:51,697 --> 00:41:52,740
You want the gold?

880
00:41:52,824 --> 00:41:54,158
[Woogy] Then fucking move!

881
00:41:54,242 --> 00:41:55,827
-No, you can't! You can't!
-[Woogy] Get off!

882
00:41:55,910 --> 00:41:57,787
[Hoonseok] I can talk to him!

883
00:41:57,870 --> 00:41:59,497
I can say you were thieves!
He won't know about the gold!

884
00:41:59,580 --> 00:42:01,791
[Heeju] Yeah! L-let him take him
to the hospital.

885
00:42:01,874 --> 00:42:03,751
After that, we can let
Hoonseok take care of it.

886
00:42:03,835 --> 00:42:05,336
Enough. Move out of the way.

887
00:42:05,419 --> 00:42:07,130
[all shouting]

888
00:42:07,213 --> 00:42:10,216
If you kill my boss,
then you'll have to kill me, too!

889
00:42:10,299 --> 00:42:11,592
Or else I'll spill everything I know!

890
00:42:11,676 --> 00:42:13,469
[Heeju] If you do this,

891
00:42:13,553 --> 00:42:16,264
then you and I are through!
You gonna kill me as well?

892
00:42:16,347 --> 00:42:18,850
[all breathing heavily]

893
00:42:18,933 --> 00:42:21,936
[Heeju] Woogy. Woogy, please.

894
00:42:23,354 --> 00:42:24,814
You always used to listen to me.

895
00:42:24,897 --> 00:42:26,774
[Heeju] When we were kids.

896
00:42:28,776 --> 00:42:29,777
[Heeju] At the coal mine.

897
00:42:29,861 --> 00:42:31,487
And I fell down.

898
00:42:32,280 --> 00:42:34,490
It was you who saved me, right?

899
00:42:35,741 --> 00:42:37,160
[both breathing heavily]

900
00:42:37,243 --> 00:42:38,786
That's right.

901
00:42:39,704 --> 00:42:41,455
I remember.

902
00:42:41,539 --> 00:42:42,582
It's just...

903
00:42:44,458 --> 00:42:45,793
...I didn't wanna remember it.

904
00:42:53,759 --> 00:42:55,052
Fuck.

905
00:42:55,136 --> 00:42:56,429
[tool clanging]

906
00:42:56,512 --> 00:42:59,557
[relieved heavy breaths]

907
00:43:11,444 --> 00:43:13,905
-Whoa, no!
-[Woogy] Hey! What?

908
00:43:13,988 --> 00:43:15,114
We're taking him to the hospital, right?

909
00:43:15,948 --> 00:43:19,744
[Hoonseok] Wait, wait, wait!
Behind your back, you-you have a knife.

910
00:43:20,828 --> 00:43:22,830
[Woogy exhales sharply]
Fuck.

911
00:43:28,002 --> 00:43:31,005
[strained breathing]

912
00:43:32,048 --> 00:43:35,426
Ah, fuck these damn
conscientious assholes.

913
00:43:35,509 --> 00:43:38,054
[labored breathing]

914
00:43:38,137 --> 00:43:39,597
[Woogy] Oh, what the fuck am I doing?

915
00:43:40,264 --> 00:43:42,225
[Woogy breathing heavily]

916
00:43:43,059 --> 00:43:44,268
[Woogy] Is this even right?

917
00:43:44,894 --> 00:43:48,731
[Woogy] Ah, what is this shit? Ah!

918
00:43:48,814 --> 00:43:51,359
[electricity buzzing]

919
00:43:51,442 --> 00:43:54,445
[machines rumbling]

920
00:43:56,656 --> 00:43:57,698
[metal clangs]

921
00:43:58,699 --> 00:44:02,078
[hammer clinking]

922
00:44:22,765 --> 00:44:24,558
[gold bars clinking]
STYLE
::cue()

923
00:44:27,979 --> 00:44:32,066
[clinking]

924
00:44:42,118 --> 00:44:43,911
[Hoonseok] Okay.

925
00:44:43,995 --> 00:44:46,831
If they're off by point-one gram,
there's no need to worry.

926
00:44:46,914 --> 00:44:51,127
That's within the normal weight range,
so you'll sell them without any issues.

927
00:44:51,210 --> 00:44:54,338
As for the leftover dust and fragments,
I'll keep them here,

928
00:44:54,422 --> 00:44:56,549
and I'll mix them in when I do
the next casting.

929
00:44:56,632 --> 00:44:57,800
[Heeju exhales]

930
00:44:57,883 --> 00:44:59,593
Thank you so much.
You did good work.

931
00:45:00,678 --> 00:45:02,096
Nice work.

932
00:45:02,179 --> 00:45:03,889
I'll be back in three days, 'kay?

933
00:45:03,973 --> 00:45:05,391
And the cash?

934
00:45:06,183 --> 00:45:07,310
[Woogy] Didn't we tell you?

935
00:45:08,769 --> 00:45:09,770
You didn't tell him?

936
00:45:09,854 --> 00:45:11,314
What?

937
00:45:12,356 --> 00:45:14,066
Well, it's a deferred payment.

938
00:45:14,150 --> 00:45:15,776
[Woogy] I'll settle it in three days.

939
00:45:15,860 --> 00:45:17,278
[Hoonseok] Wait, wait, wait.
Wait a minute.

940
00:45:17,361 --> 00:45:18,487
Uh, deferred?

941
00:45:18,571 --> 00:45:20,406
Come on.

942
00:45:21,324 --> 00:45:22,491
Shit, you don't trust us?

943
00:45:22,575 --> 00:45:24,452
Of course I don't trust you!

944
00:45:24,535 --> 00:45:27,580
How do I know you two will actually
come back in three days?

945
00:45:27,663 --> 00:45:29,206
Well, what do you want?

946
00:45:29,290 --> 00:45:30,541
[Woogy] I don't have it!
I don't have the cash!

947
00:45:30,624 --> 00:45:33,836
Hold on. We-we agreed
to give you two percent, didn't we?

948
00:45:33,919 --> 00:45:35,087
Yeah.

949
00:45:36,797 --> 00:45:37,798
[Heeju] Well, this...

950
00:45:37,882 --> 00:45:39,175
[grunts]

951
00:45:39,258 --> 00:45:41,344
...is worth 150 mil.

952
00:45:41,427 --> 00:45:43,346
[Heeju] Consider this half upfront.

953
00:45:43,429 --> 00:45:46,182
And you'll get the rest once
the job is done.

954
00:45:47,099 --> 00:45:48,100
Oh.

955
00:45:50,061 --> 00:45:53,272
Wow. You really scored.

956
00:45:54,023 --> 00:45:55,316
Lucky you.

957
00:45:56,025 --> 00:45:58,152
Give it to me.
I'll exchange it for you.

958
00:45:58,235 --> 00:46:01,280
No, thanks.
I can take care of it myself.

959
00:46:02,490 --> 00:46:05,951
And you'll promise us that you'll be able
to work on the rest, too?

960
00:46:07,203 --> 00:46:09,830
Yes, Boss.
I'll do it because I trust you.

961
00:46:09,914 --> 00:46:10,915
[relieved exhale]

962
00:46:11,832 --> 00:46:14,043
But I don't trust him at all.

963
00:46:14,126 --> 00:46:17,838
You motherfucker. You think you can point
your finger and say that shit to my face?

964
00:46:17,922 --> 00:46:19,382
[Woogy] Who the fuck do you think you are?

965
00:46:19,465 --> 00:46:20,549
-You wanna die?
-See you next time.

966
00:46:20,633 --> 00:46:22,385
What a piece of shit.
Hey, hey!

967
00:46:22,468 --> 00:46:24,261
[Woogy] I don't trust you either, you
prick!

968
00:46:24,345 --> 00:46:26,847
-[Woogy] Where's my knife? No!
-[Heeju] Stop it. Come on. Come on.

969
00:46:35,189 --> 00:46:36,190
Sorry.

970
00:46:37,316 --> 00:46:39,193
I got worked up earlier.

971
00:46:40,820 --> 00:46:43,155
The whole situation kinda got out
of control.

972
00:46:46,450 --> 00:46:47,701
Do you need a doctor?

973
00:46:48,577 --> 00:46:49,578
Forget it.

974
00:46:50,496 --> 00:46:52,540
Instead, I need your word.

975
00:46:53,374 --> 00:46:57,169
If you and I are going to work together,
you won't kill anyone.

976
00:46:57,253 --> 00:47:01,340
[Heeju] If you ever pull a knife
or spill blood one more time,

977
00:47:01,424 --> 00:47:03,217
you and I are done.
It's over.

978
00:47:04,427 --> 00:47:05,428
[Woogy scoffs]

979
00:47:07,471 --> 00:47:09,473
What if someone finds out
we're doing this?

980
00:47:13,352 --> 00:47:14,353
[inhales and exhales sharply]

981
00:47:14,437 --> 00:47:16,897
You think you're being
fucking conscientious?

982
00:47:16,981 --> 00:47:17,982
Hmm?

983
00:47:20,526 --> 00:47:22,361
That mindset doesn't make
any fucking sense

984
00:47:22,445 --> 00:47:23,571
for a wannabe thief.

985
00:47:24,488 --> 00:47:28,033
[Woogy] Fuck.
You're stealing gold, you know.

986
00:47:28,117 --> 00:47:30,661
A whopping 100 kilograms
of someone else's gold.

987
00:47:31,370 --> 00:47:34,582
And now you want the money?
All in good conscience?

988
00:47:34,665 --> 00:47:36,500
[Woogy] Without getting blood
on your hands?

989
00:47:37,877 --> 00:47:39,336
[exhales sharply]

990
00:47:42,006 --> 00:47:43,716
Well, then.

991
00:47:43,799 --> 00:47:45,509
Do you promise or not?

992
00:47:47,470 --> 00:47:48,762
[exhales sharply]

993
00:47:48,846 --> 00:47:50,347
Yeah, I'll do my best.

994
00:47:50,431 --> 00:47:53,434
[♪ dramatic music]

995
00:47:59,273 --> 00:48:00,274
[Woogy] Here.
STYLE
::cue()

996
00:48:13,913 --> 00:48:14,997
[exhales]

997
00:48:18,042 --> 00:48:21,045
[distant birds chirping]

998
00:48:21,128 --> 00:48:24,131
[♪ dramatic music continues]

999
00:48:40,314 --> 00:48:41,941
[door creaks open]

1000
00:48:50,449 --> 00:48:51,450
[Heeju gasps]

1001
00:48:51,534 --> 00:48:52,910
[shuddering]

1002
00:48:52,993 --> 00:48:54,620
[Sunok] How much longer
are you gonna sleep?

1003
00:48:54,703 --> 00:48:56,539
It's already dark out.

1004
00:48:57,581 --> 00:48:58,999
Keep still.

1005
00:49:00,417 --> 00:49:01,418
[Sunok] Almost done.

1006
00:49:16,016 --> 00:49:17,017
Go.

1007
00:49:18,769 --> 00:49:20,145
Get out of here.

1008
00:49:22,189 --> 00:49:23,440
[Sunok] Run away.

1009
00:49:23,524 --> 00:49:25,359
I'll pay off all of your debt for you.

1010
00:49:26,277 --> 00:49:28,862
Do you even have the money
to pay off my debt?

1011
00:49:29,488 --> 00:49:30,698
You don't even know what I owe.

1012
00:49:31,782 --> 00:49:33,242
How much is it?

1013
00:49:33,325 --> 00:49:34,618
[exhales sharply]

1014
00:49:36,287 --> 00:49:37,580
I don't have debt.

1015
00:49:39,039 --> 00:49:41,125
When it's time, I'll leave quietly.
Don't worry.

1016
00:49:42,126 --> 00:49:43,168
Where were you last night?

1017
00:49:45,296 --> 00:49:46,922
Were you hanging out with that thug?

1018
00:49:48,215 --> 00:49:50,259
-What on Earth did you do with your hand?
-I already told you,

1019
00:49:50,342 --> 00:49:51,719
there's nothing going on!

1020
00:49:53,095 --> 00:49:54,179
And my hand...

1021
00:49:55,389 --> 00:49:56,849
I just fell, okay?

1022
00:49:56,932 --> 00:49:58,892
Don't tell me it was from a fall!
It was from a knife.

1023
00:49:58,976 --> 00:50:00,311
Enough, all right.

1024
00:50:01,228 --> 00:50:03,772
Wow. You luckless bitch.

1025
00:50:03,856 --> 00:50:04,898
[surprised exhale]

1026
00:50:04,982 --> 00:50:07,067
You ran away and still ended up like this.

1027
00:50:09,194 --> 00:50:10,237
[both exhale]

1028
00:50:11,655 --> 00:50:13,699
You wanna know what's really ridiculous?

1029
00:50:14,742 --> 00:50:18,621
Everyone can tell that the bitch
with the worst luck is you.

1030
00:50:19,997 --> 00:50:22,708
So hearing you call me that
just makes me furious.

1031
00:50:23,751 --> 00:50:25,336
It really pisses me off.

1032
00:50:28,631 --> 00:50:30,633
Don't put all your trust
into men like that.

1033
00:50:32,259 --> 00:50:34,178
One moment can ruin your whole life.

1034
00:50:34,261 --> 00:50:35,679
You're one to talk.

1035
00:50:35,763 --> 00:50:38,015
Then why did you marry that trash?

1036
00:50:38,098 --> 00:50:39,725
[Sunok] To survive.

1037
00:50:39,808 --> 00:50:42,227
You think I could pay off my debt
and raise a kid by serving coffee?

1038
00:50:42,311 --> 00:50:44,521
-If it weren't for you I would've...
-[Heeju] Don't use me as an excuse!

1039
00:50:44,605 --> 00:50:46,357
I never asked for any of that!

1040
00:50:47,816 --> 00:50:50,069
Every single moment I had to spend
with that man was nothing but hell!

1041
00:50:50,152 --> 00:50:51,236
An do you think I was happy?

1042
00:50:51,320 --> 00:50:53,989
That's why I begged you to run away!

1043
00:50:54,073 --> 00:50:55,324
[Heeju] You didn't wanna go, though!

1044
00:50:55,407 --> 00:50:57,576
[Heeju] Even after I told you what
that man tried to do to me, you...

1045
00:50:57,660 --> 00:50:59,828
[Sunok] What is the point
of dredging this up now?

1046
00:50:59,912 --> 00:51:01,455
Should I beg for your forgiveness?

1047
00:51:01,538 --> 00:51:03,082
-Would that make it better?
-[Heeju] Yes!

1048
00:51:03,999 --> 00:51:05,501
Beg and apologize.

1049
00:51:05,584 --> 00:51:07,169
So I can feel better.

1050
00:51:07,252 --> 00:51:08,754
[labored breathing]

1051
00:51:13,842 --> 00:51:17,012
[door opens and closes]

1052
00:51:17,096 --> 00:51:20,015
[whimpering]

1053
00:51:20,099 --> 00:51:23,102
[crying]

1054
00:51:30,609 --> 00:51:33,612
[pills rattling]

1055
00:51:47,251 --> 00:51:50,254
[panicked breathing]

1056
00:51:51,672 --> 00:51:53,215
[Sunok] Heeju, Heeju.
Don't come out.

1057
00:51:53,298 --> 00:51:54,717
[Sunok] Your uncle is here.
[door closes]

1058
00:51:59,805 --> 00:52:02,683
[door opens]

1059
00:52:05,310 --> 00:52:07,396
Well? You glad to see me?

1060
00:52:07,479 --> 00:52:08,897
It's been two months.

1061
00:52:08,981 --> 00:52:12,359
Uh, I was about to close up here.

1062
00:52:13,652 --> 00:52:15,946
[Sunok] Let's go home.
Did you eat?

1063
00:52:21,869 --> 00:52:23,120
[Cheoljung] Get in here already.

1064
00:52:26,331 --> 00:52:29,418
Hi. It's me again.
[chuckles]

1065
00:52:29,501 --> 00:52:31,587
[door creaks]
STYLE
::cue()

1066
00:52:33,922 --> 00:52:37,843
[Cheoljung] So I heard you sold a watch
to Mr. Jang a week ago.

1067
00:52:37,926 --> 00:52:39,720
For 30 million.

1068
00:52:40,971 --> 00:52:42,973
[exhales]
How much did you pay for it?

1069
00:52:43,891 --> 00:52:45,768
You were able to sell for a high price.

1070
00:52:45,851 --> 00:52:47,394
And you didn't tell me.

1071
00:52:47,478 --> 00:52:49,313
[Mr. Jang clears throat]

1072
00:52:49,396 --> 00:52:54,151
I mean, I thought the price was, well,
a little too high.

1073
00:52:54,234 --> 00:52:55,736
So I let Han know.

1074
00:52:56,820 --> 00:52:58,155
All right, bring me the ledger.

1075
00:52:59,281 --> 00:53:02,284
[Cheoljung] I said bring me the ledger.

1076
00:53:02,367 --> 00:53:05,204
[♪ suspenseful music]

1077
00:53:21,053 --> 00:53:22,429
[exhales]

1078
00:53:22,513 --> 00:53:24,181
What else did you say you took?

1079
00:53:24,973 --> 00:53:27,476
[Mr. Jang] That's all for this month.
Wait, actually,

1080
00:53:27,559 --> 00:53:29,520
I bought a few rings, too.

1081
00:53:29,603 --> 00:53:31,480
I think she priced those correctly.

1082
00:53:31,563 --> 00:53:32,815
[Mr. Jang chuckles]

1083
00:53:33,899 --> 00:53:35,567
You said you got diamonds.

1084
00:53:35,651 --> 00:53:37,861
'Bout a month ago.

1085
00:53:41,824 --> 00:53:43,033
[Cheoljung exhales]

1086
00:53:43,116 --> 00:53:44,159
No diamonds.

1087
00:53:45,202 --> 00:53:47,120
Not even one.

1088
00:53:52,334 --> 00:53:54,753
Is there a separate ledger for Janggak?

1089
00:53:59,216 --> 00:54:00,425
[book lands on desk]

1090
00:54:02,928 --> 00:54:04,429
[cigarette sizzles]

1091
00:54:05,138 --> 00:54:06,431
You can go home now.

1092
00:54:07,641 --> 00:54:09,142
[groans]

1093
00:54:09,226 --> 00:54:12,354
I hope I didn't say anything that
was unnecessary.

1094
00:54:12,437 --> 00:54:14,523
No, you were right to.

1095
00:54:14,606 --> 00:54:16,650
I'm the owner and the husband.

1096
00:54:17,317 --> 00:54:19,152
-Best that I know everything.
-Right.

1097
00:54:19,236 --> 00:54:21,321
[Cheoljung] All right, then.
Take care.

1098
00:54:21,405 --> 00:54:22,656
[Cheoljung exhales]

1099
00:54:23,574 --> 00:54:25,117
Uh, I'll see you.

1100
00:54:25,200 --> 00:54:26,326
[Cheoljung] Goodbye.

1101
00:54:27,119 --> 00:54:29,079
[door creaks]

1102
00:54:29,162 --> 00:54:30,205
[locks click]

1103
00:54:31,039 --> 00:54:33,208
[cigarette sizzles]

1104
00:54:34,668 --> 00:54:35,836
[exhales]

1105
00:54:39,506 --> 00:54:41,675
[Cheoljung] You must
have really lost your mind.

1106
00:54:42,801 --> 00:54:45,137
[inhales on cigarette]

1107
00:54:45,220 --> 00:54:48,432
You were just a coffee shop girl
with a little kid.

1108
00:54:48,515 --> 00:54:50,434
I took you in and fed you,

1109
00:54:50,517 --> 00:54:53,061
and you thank me
by taking my money on the sly?

1110
00:54:53,145 --> 00:54:54,730
[inhales]

1111
00:54:54,813 --> 00:54:56,398
[exhales]

1112
00:54:57,357 --> 00:54:58,358
[stomps out cigarette]

1113
00:55:02,863 --> 00:55:04,239
When did this start?

1114
00:55:06,366 --> 00:55:08,160
How much have you skimmed now?

1115
00:55:11,038 --> 00:55:12,831
-That's all.
-[Sunok] Oh.

1116
00:55:13,957 --> 00:55:15,626
Really?

1117
00:55:17,461 --> 00:55:20,672
[Cheoljung exhales sharply]
You thieving bitch.

1118
00:55:21,423 --> 00:55:24,301
Look at you still lying through
your fucking teeth!

1119
00:55:24,384 --> 00:55:25,385
[slams hand on table]

1120
00:55:30,474 --> 00:55:31,516
[Cheoljung] Shit!

1121
00:55:32,726 --> 00:55:35,062
-[panicked breathing]
-[grunting]

1122
00:55:35,145 --> 00:55:36,146
Where do you think you're going?

1123
00:55:36,229 --> 00:55:37,648
-[screaming]
-[Cheoljung] Come here!

1124
00:55:37,731 --> 00:55:39,900
[both shouting]

1125
00:55:39,983 --> 00:55:41,234
[filing cabinet bangs]

1126
00:55:41,318 --> 00:55:44,780
[Sunok groaning]

1127
00:55:45,697 --> 00:55:47,824
Better not say you fucking spent it all.

1128
00:55:47,908 --> 00:55:51,203
If you did, I swear I'll
send you straight to Heaven.

1129
00:55:52,496 --> 00:55:53,997
[gasping]

1130
00:55:54,081 --> 00:55:55,082
I swear.

1131
00:55:55,165 --> 00:55:57,292
[gagging]

1132
00:55:57,376 --> 00:55:58,710
[Sunok struggling]

1133
00:55:58,794 --> 00:56:00,420
Hah!

1134
00:56:00,504 --> 00:56:03,757
[groaning]

1135
00:56:04,341 --> 00:56:05,926
[gasps]

1136
00:56:07,594 --> 00:56:08,762
You won't say?

1137
00:56:08,845 --> 00:56:11,932
[Cheoljung] You know I won't hesitate
to cut you.

1138
00:56:12,015 --> 00:56:14,017
I am gonna check the ledgers.

1139
00:56:14,101 --> 00:56:17,104
So why don't you just spit it out,
fucking bitch?

1140
00:56:21,358 --> 00:56:23,151
[blow lands]
[groans]

1141
00:56:23,235 --> 00:56:24,778
-[Cheoljung groans]
-[Sunok gasps]

1142
00:56:26,488 --> 00:56:30,033
No, Heeju!
No, don't do it.

1143
00:56:30,117 --> 00:56:32,869
[Heeju whimpering]

1144
00:56:32,953 --> 00:56:34,121
[Sunok gasps]

1145
00:56:34,204 --> 00:56:37,040
[blood squelching]

1146
00:56:37,124 --> 00:56:40,001
[both breathing heavily]

1147
00:56:42,421 --> 00:56:45,257
[Sunok] Go.
Hurry, hurry, go.

1148
00:56:45,340 --> 00:56:47,175
Look at me and get a hold of yourself!

1149
00:56:47,259 --> 00:56:49,219
Just grab what you need and go.

1150
00:56:49,302 --> 00:56:50,554
I'll take care of everything.
STYLE
::cue()

1151
00:56:53,765 --> 00:56:57,310
[drawers clanging]

1152
00:57:01,189 --> 00:57:04,192
[both breathing heavily]

1153
00:57:13,285 --> 00:57:15,537
[Sunok] Take this.
It's the money I've earned over the years.

1154
00:57:16,580 --> 00:57:17,914
I've been saving it for you.

1155
00:57:20,083 --> 00:57:22,544
So take it and don't ever come back.

1156
00:57:22,627 --> 00:57:26,465
[Sunok] No matter what happens to me,
don't try to look for me.

1157
00:57:26,548 --> 00:57:27,549
Don't try to find out.

1158
00:57:28,550 --> 00:57:29,926
You go somewhere far away.

1159
00:57:30,969 --> 00:57:32,596
I want you to live a good life.

1160
00:57:33,597 --> 00:57:34,598
No.

1161
00:57:35,891 --> 00:57:37,851
You have to go.

1162
00:57:37,934 --> 00:57:40,562
I'm really sorry.
Heeju.

1163
00:57:40,645 --> 00:57:42,689
[Sunok] I'm sorry.

1164
00:57:42,773 --> 00:57:45,317
I need you to listen.
Just listen to me this once.

1165
00:57:45,400 --> 00:57:47,444
Go! You going will save my life.

1166
00:57:47,527 --> 00:57:49,821
[Sunok] Go. Go!

1167
00:57:49,905 --> 00:57:51,823
[Heeju] Auntie! Auntie!

1168
00:57:51,907 --> 00:57:52,908
-[Sunok] Go!
-[Heeju] Auntie!

1169
00:57:52,991 --> 00:57:54,993
[Heeju crying]

1170
00:57:55,076 --> 00:57:58,497
I told you to go! Go!
Hurry up and get outta here!

1171
00:58:00,373 --> 00:58:02,834
[Sunok] I said go away! Go!

1172
00:58:02,918 --> 00:58:06,379
[both crying]

1173
00:58:06,463 --> 00:58:10,091
[whimpering]

1174
00:58:14,554 --> 00:58:17,182
[sniffling]

1175
00:58:33,156 --> 00:58:36,326
[cell phone trilling]

1176
00:58:36,409 --> 00:58:37,410
[receiver clicks]

1177
00:58:37,494 --> 00:58:39,162
[gasps]

1178
00:58:39,246 --> 00:58:40,247
Hello.

1179
00:58:40,789 --> 00:58:43,834
I-I'm in Bukju.

1180
00:58:45,544 --> 00:58:47,504
[Sunok] The Happy Pawnshop in Bukju.

1181
00:58:48,839 --> 00:58:52,676
[Sunok] I think I killed a person.

1182
00:59:00,308 --> 00:59:03,311
[crying]

1183
00:59:19,452 --> 00:59:20,912
[distant sirens wailing]

1184
00:59:20,996 --> 00:59:23,999
[sirens approaching]

1185
00:59:26,418 --> 00:59:28,044
[tires squeaking]

1186
00:59:32,257 --> 00:59:34,467
[more sirens approaching]

1187
00:59:34,551 --> 00:59:36,011
[brakes squeaking]

1188
00:59:36,094 --> 00:59:37,304
Auntie.

1189
00:59:37,387 --> 00:59:39,639
[crying]

1190
00:59:39,723 --> 00:59:40,849
Mom.

1191
00:59:40,932 --> 00:59:43,935
[crying]

1192
00:59:47,856 --> 00:59:50,734
[sirens wailing]

1193
00:59:50,817 --> 00:59:53,820
[Heeju crying]

1194
00:59:53,904 --> 00:59:56,907
[♪ dramatic music]

1195
01:00:23,266 --> 01:00:26,269
[♪ dramatic music continues]

